From 75a0f3c4d16e5caaa03032e94faf4082f4533bfc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 23:35:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] pthreadpool: declare AROS aligned allocation [chromium]
 [aros]

Statement:
The strict GNU11 pthreadpool allocation unit calls AROS posix_memalign, but the target C library does not expose its prototype through the generic stdlib header in this feature-test configuration.

Decision:
Declare the existing POSIX ABI only for AROS at the vendor boundary. Keep pthreadpool allocation and matching free semantics unchanged.

Evidence:
The original memory.o failed with an implicit declaration error. obj/third_party/pthreadpool/pthreadpool/memory.o compiles after the declaration.

Chain:

---
 src/memory.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/memory.c b/src/memory.c
index fc0d83e..2d031a7 100644
--- a/src/memory.c
+++ b/src/memory.c
@@ -4,6 +4,10 @@
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <string.h>
 
+#ifdef __AROS__
+extern int posix_memalign(void** memptr, size_t alignment, size_t size);
+#endif
+
 /* POSIX headers */
 #ifdef __ANDROID__
 	#include <malloc.h>
